pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Regression test: `GeneralPBConstraint::add` promotes an i64 accumulator to i128 when the
% sums no longer fit into i64, and that branch subtracted the cancellation in i128 after
% checking only the unadjusted sums. The degree sum is i128::MIN + 1 and merging `2 x3`
% with `2 ~x3` cancels 2, so the true degree is i128::MIN - 1. The formula is satisfiable
% (x2, x3 true).
f 2 ;
pol 1 2 + ;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT : 3 ;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
